{"id":"mistral-missile","slug":"mistral-missile","name":"Mistral","aliases":["Sadral","MBDA Mistral","Simbad missile","Mistral missile","Mistral surface-to-air missile","Mistral (missile)"],"kind":"missile","category":"manpads","subcategory":"French short range air defense system","description":"The Missile Transportable Anti-aérien Léger, commonly called Mistral, is a family of French infrared homing multipurpose short range air defense system manufactured by MBDA France. Based on the French SATCP, the development of the portable system that would later become the Mistral began in 1974. The first version of the system was introduced in 1990, the second in 1998, and the third in 2013.","history":"Mistral missiles used by the Rwandan forces in the Second Congo War shot down a Zimbabwean Air Force BAE Hawk fighter on 23 March 1999.\nTwo automated SADRAL launchers (re-cycled from the retiring Georges Leygues-class frigates) and each equipped with six Mistral Mk 3 surface-to-air missiles were fitted to three La Fayette-class frigates of the French Navy in the 2021–2023 period. The system replaced the previous Crotale system in order to provide a modernized defence against sea-skimming targets.\nThe Mistral Mk 3 carries an infrared imaging seeker and possesses advanced image processing capabilities. This allows it to engage low thermal signature targets such as: UAVs, turbojet-powered missiles and fast craft at long range, while reportedly offering resistance to countermeasures. The system is also carried on the aircraft carrier Charles de Gaulle, the Mistral-class amphibious assault ships and (SIMBAD-RC) is being installed on the French Navy's Jacques Chevallier-class support ships.\nTwo Sadral turrets for Mistral were also installed on the raised deck on each side of the helicopter hangar of the former Cassard-class frigates. Space for the SADRAL/Mistral system is also provided for on the French Horizon-class frigates, and as of 2025, is to be fit to these vessels, as well as to all French Aquitaine and FDI-class frigates.\nNorway sent 100 Mistral systems to Ukraine shortly after the start of the Russian invasion of Ukraine.  In response to the need for faster weapon shipments as a result of the war, in early 2023 MBDA started accelerating production of the Mistral 3 from 20 to 30 missiles per month, and to 40 per month by late 2023.","facts":[],"specifications":[{"group":"Warhead","items":[{"label":"Detonation Mechanism","value":"Laser proximity or impact triggered"}]},{"group":"Propulsion & Guidance","items":[{"label":"Engine","value":"Solid Rocket Motor, 2-stage"},{"label":"Guidance","value":"Infrared homing"}]},{"group":"Dimensions","items":[{"label":"Weight","value":"19.7 kg","numeric":19.7,"unit":"kg"},{"label":"Length","value":"1.86 m","numeric":1.86,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Length","value":"1.88m (including initial booster)","numeric":1.88,"unit":"m"},{"label":"Diameter","value":"90 mm","numeric":90,"unit":"mm"}]},{"group":"Performance","items":[{"label":"Operational Range","value":"8 km (Mistral 3)","numeric":8,"unit":"km"},{"label":"Speed","value":"930 m/s, approx. Mach 2.71 (high supersonic)","numeric":930,"unit":"m/s"},{"label":"Flight Ceiling","value":"6 km (Mistral 3)","numeric":6,"unit":"km"}]},{"group":"Production","items":[{"label":"Designer","value":"Matra Défense (now merged into MBDA)"},{"label":"Designed","value":"1974 onwards"},{"label":"Manufacturer","value":"MBDA France"},{"label":"Unit Cost (Mistral 3)","value":"US$545,600 (2024)"}]},{"group":"Service","items":[{"label":"Origin","value":"France"},{"label":"In Service","value":"1990–present"}]}],"specIndex":{"Detonation Mechanism":"Laser proximity or impact triggered","Engine":"Solid Rocket Motor, 2-stage","Guidance":"Infrared homing","Weight":"19.7 kg","Length":"1.86 m","Diameter":"90 mm","Operational Range":"8 km (Mistral 3)","Speed":"930 m/s, approx. Mach 2.71 (high supersonic)","Flight Ceiling":"6 km (Mistral 3)","Designer":"Matra Défense (now merged into MBDA)","Designed":"1974 onwards","Manufacturer":"MBDA France","Unit Cost":"US$545,600 (2024)","Origin":"France","In Service":"1990–present"},"images":{"hero":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/2c/Mistral_Atlas_launcher_of_the_Hungarian_Armed_Forces_cropped.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mistral_Atlas_launcher_of_the_Hungarian_Armed_Forces_cropped.jpg","width":940,"height":904,"license":"CC0","licenseUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","attribution":"Admiralis-generalis-Aladeen"},"thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Mistral_Atlas_launcher_of_the_Hungarian_Armed_Forces_cropped.jpg/330px-Mistral_Atlas_launcher_of_the_Hungarian_Armed_Forces_cropped.jpg"},"gallery":[{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0e/KRI_Frans_Kaisiepo-368_Heli_Ops_Passex_Mediterranean_Sea%2C_March_2023.jpg","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KRI_Frans_Kaisiepo-368_Heli_Ops_Passex_Mediterranean_Sea,_March_2023.jpg","width":5184,"height":3456,"caption":"Indonesian navy helicopter AS565 Panther (HS-1306) performing aerial photo and Intelligence, Surveillance & Reconnaissance (ISR) operation during passing exercise with ITS Andrea Doria D-553 of the Italian navy in Mediterranean Sea. (March 10, 2023)","license":"Public domain","attribution":"PPID Tentara Nasional Indonesia"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c4/MBDA_Mistral_-_IDET_2017.JPG","descriptionUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MBDA_Mistral_-_IDET_2017.JPG","width":4884,"height":3221,"caption":"Missile of the MBDA's Mistral man-portable air-defense systems (MANPADS). IDET 2017, Brno Exhibition Center, Czech Republic.","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","attribution":"Karel Šubrt"},{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7f/2021-02-26_Simbad-RC_on_BRP_Antonio_Luna.jpg","descriptionUrl":"htt